## Summary

| Severity | Count | Top Issue |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| 🔴 Critical | 4 | LINQ chains allocating enumerators/delegates/closures on every call |
| 🟡 Moderate | 4 | `params` array, `.ToLower()`, unsealed classes, substring slice |

The dominant cost is the **LINQ pipeline in `FromPascalCase`** (finding #1) and the **double-humanization in `Dehumanize → Pascalize`** (finding #3). Fixing these two alone would eliminate the majority of per-call allocations. For a CMS rendering hundreds of strings, this could mean **thousands fewer allocations per page render**.

